## 6. Architecture Boundaries

Before scaffolding code, define the initial feature/layer map in [Architecture Layering v0.1](./architecture-layering-v0.1.md).

Rules that should hold from the first implementation:

- lower layers must not import runtime, UI, transport, persistence, provider SDK, or framework boundary concerns unless that layer owns the boundary.
- cross-cutting concerns should enter through explicit providers or interfaces.
- hand-written product source files should stay at or below 300 lines; split by layer, route, component, or helper before exceeding that limit.

## 7. Validation Strategy

Use `./scripts/finalize.sh` as the final check-only gate for implementation work.

Run `./scripts/smoke.sh` after changes to startup, routing, environment wiring, or cross-service integration.

